                     {:git/url \\\"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\\\"\\n                                       :sha \\\"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\\\"}\\n                                      }}\\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]\\n                  :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"cljd.build\\\"]\\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \\\"2.8.0\\\"}}\\n                    :jvm-opts [\\\"-Dconfig=config.clj\\\"]\\n     the roster allows), stop dispatching: record both failures in the work\\n     log with their artifact trails and escalate to the user with the\\n     evidence. A third model is chosen only on user instruction — an\\n     unbounded retry loop is the failure mode this rule exists to end.\\n6. **Verify — individual tests may run locally; suites run remotely (owner\\n   ruling 2026-11-04).** Inspect the actual artifact and diff in the\\n   orchestrator's environment. An individual test is fast: a single failing\\n   test or one namespace's reproduction (`-v <ns>/<var>`, `-n <ns>`,\\n   `--test=<ns>`, `--only <ns>`) may run on the laptop. Everything\\n   suite-scale — subsystem lane sets (G1), changed-set runs (G2), full\\n   suites, the slow tier, the nightly — runs on the remote hosts\\n   (shiva/jupiter): the suite has outgrown the laptop, and local suite runs\\n   are too slow and load the machine the owner is using. Delegate agents\\n   (`claude`, `codex`, `glm`, …) can execute on the remote test hosts\\n   directly — see [`build-n-test.md`](../build-n-test.md), section \\\"Remote\\n   agent execution\\\" (the laptop-unload rule: bookkeeping locally, execution\\n   remotely) and \\\"Remote test servers\\\" for the host recipes (scratch clones\\n   under `~/ci/`, mise activation order, per-host lane overlap limits).\\n   Delegated test claims are untrusted: the orchestrator reads the\\n   remote run's actual output (log paths on the host), not the delegate's\\n   summary. User-run results count as evidence only when the exact command,\\n   output, and tested revision are available; otherwise run the checks.\\n   Tell later reviewers which checks already passed so they spend their\\n   budget on static analysis instead of redundant suites, except when\\n   security review requires a rerun.\\n7. **Review and reconcile.** Give the verified diff to an independent reviewer\\n   before committing (exceptions: the coordination contract's user waiver and\\n   trivial-edit exemption). Weigh findings on their merits, fix accepted\\n   defects, and resume the same reviewer to confirm the correction. Preserve\\n   every round. Findings are reconciled when every one carries a recorded\\n   disposition: fixed and reviewer-confirmed, rejected with evidence, or\\n   deferred with user approval. A reviewer–architect dispute is terminated by\\n   one architect adjudication per unit: the ruling is final for that unit,\\n   and residual disagreement is recorded as an unresolved risk in the step 8\\n   readiness report — never re-litigated by re-dispatching review rounds.\\n8. **Report readiness.** Report exact commands, assertion counts, reviewer\\n   sign-off, unrun checks, unreviewed changes, unresolved risks, and any tool or\\n   hook noise. Do not let the summary outrun the evidence. Append the unit's\\n   entry to this session's own file under `orchestrator-logs/` in the same terms.\\n9. **Stage, commit, and merge only when authorized** under the coordination\\n   contract's commit authority. Stage only the authorized work, inspect the\\n   staged diff immediately before committing, and commit only that diff.\\n   Use the commit message format in\\n   [`format.md`](../format.md#git-commit-messages). Before staging in the\\n   shared main tree, re-run `git status` and compare against the state\\n   derived in step 2: any working-tree change not attributable to this\\n   seat's units (another seat's or the user's in-flight work) freezes the\\n   commit — escalate, never stage around it, and never `git add -A` in the\\n   main tree.\\n10. **Verify what landed.** Compare the commit's diff with the authorized\\n    staged diff. If hooks or formatters changed what landed, review that delta and\\n    rerun its affected checks — the pre-commit formatter hook can stage files\\n    you never added (observed 2026-10-26: an untracked in-flight file of\\n    another track was swept into a ledger commit; caught only by reading the\\n    post-commit `--stat` against intent). A failure means the work is not\\n    ready; rewrite history only as the coordination contract allows.\\n    **Shared append-only ledgers (`docs/agents/known-gaps.md`) have a merge\\n    rule** (2026-10-26, after merge 4d6fd818 silently dropped ~66 rows by\\n    replacing the file with a rewritten 16-row variant): never resolve a\\n    ledger conflict by taking one side's file, and never land a rewritten or\\n    reformatted ledger inside a feature merge. The ledger is append-only\\n11:  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\\n702:      (:const m) (assoc :dart/const (:const m)) ; can be :required\\n903:                         (with-meta (list ext) {:const :required})]))\\n906:                     (with-meta (list ext) {:const :required})\\n919:                         `(~(with-meta (list cname) {:const :required})))\\n3512:(defn- import-to-require [spec]\\n3520:(defn- use-to-require [spec]\\n3529:(defn- refer-clojure-to-require [refer-spec]\\n3541:(defn emit-ns [[_ ns-sym & ns-clauses :as ns-form] _]\\n3556:                              :require #(if (sequential? %) % [%])\\n3607:                               :when (= :require op)\\n3629:              (list :require (into [host-ns] cat options))))\\n3816:           :required\\n3817:           (throw (ex-info \\\"^{:const :required} but expression is not const.\\\"\\n3819:           (println \\\"🤔 WARNING: Unexpected ^:const, IGNORING IT. Remove it or use ^{:const :required} to assert.\\\" (pr-str x) (source-info))))\\n3822:       (when (and const inferred-const (not= const :required))\\n3823:         (println \\\"🤔 INFO: Useless ^:const, please remove or use ^{:const :required} to assert.\\\"\\n4934:             (let [form (read {:eof in :read-cond :allow :features #{:cljd}} in)]\\n4951:                               :features #{:cljd :cljd/clj-host :clj}} in)]\\n4990:    [(str base \\\".cljd\\\") (str base \\\".cljc\\\")]))\\n1082:;; reader conditionals: jolt's feature set is {:jolt :clj :default}; the FIRST\\n1083:;; clause whose feature key is in the set wins (clause order, like Clojure).\\n1102:(define rdr-features '(\\\"jolt\\\" \\\"clj\\\" \\\"default\\\"))\\n1103:(define (rdr-feature? kw)\\n1105:       (and (member (keyword-t-name kw) rdr-features) #t)))\\n1106:(define rdr-reserved-features (list (keyword #f \\\"else\\\") (keyword #f \\\"none\\\")))\\n1108:;; and whitespace, and a feature that matches must be followed by its form. A\\n1109:;; feature that does not match may end the list — the reference discards the\\n1111:(define (rdr-read-reader-cond s i end)   ; i is past the '?'\\n1123:                ((memq (car xs) rdr-reserved-features)\\n1126:                ((and (null? (cdr xs)) (rdr-feature? (car xs)))\\n1134:                ((rdr-feature? (car xs))\\n1577:       (rdr-read-reader-cond s (+ i 1) end))\\n2195:;; :features are accepted and ignored: jolt's reader always resolves #?\\n2196:;; conditionals, against the fixed host feature set {:jolt :clj :default} (see\\n2197:;; rdr-features), so a reader-conditional string reads the same either way.\\n   995\\t\\n   996\\t\\n   997\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   998\\t;; Reading and classifying input\\n   999\\t;; =============================================================================\\n  1000\\t\\n  1001\\t(defn read-forms\\n  1002\\t  \\\"The forms of one input line, as a vector, read by the host reader.\\n  1003\\t   Public so the cross-host reader tests can compare the forms, metadata\\n  1004\\t   included, that each host reads.\\\"\\n  1005\\t  [input]\\n  1006\\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \\\"[\\\" input \\\"]\\\"))\\n  1007\\t     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \\\"[\\\" input \\\"]\\\"))\\n  1008\\t     :clj (clojure.core/read-string (str \\\"[\\\" input \\\"]\\\"))))\\n  1009\\t\\n  1010\\t\\n  1011\\t(defn- command-form?\\n  1012\\t  [form]\\n  1013\\t  (and (seq? form)\\n  1014\\t       (symbol? (first form))\\n  1015\\t       (contains? command-heads (first form))))\\n27:Tree: master@873c8bcd, clean\\n29:- Root-caused Shiva dart nightly failure from `collab/yang-clojure/1793905679000-orchestrator-dart-cljd-compile-break.glm-5.3-flash.findings.md`:\\n30:  1. ClojureDart matched :clj reader conditional requires in `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`, attempting to load non-existent `cljd.tools.reader` and failing on `rt/string-push-back-reader` in `read-forms`.\\n31:  2. `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc` used `defquoted` which expands to `edn/read-string` under cljd, but lacked `#?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])`.\\n32:  3. `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` required JVM Java ANTLR classes for PHP under `#?@(:clj ...)`, which ClojureDart matched without `:cljd []`.\\n33:- Landed commit `873c8bcd` (`fix(dart): add reader conditionals for ClojureDart compilation`).\\n35:- Dispatched Lead System Architect review to `gpt-6.1-sol` via Codex (`collab/yang-clojure/1793950384477-architect-dart-cljd-guards-review.prompt.md`).\\n36:- Triggered remote nightly test lanes on Shiva (`node,dart`) and Jupiter (`jvm`) under pinned commit `873c8bcd`.\\n37:Decisions: Escalate architectural review of the cross-platform reader conditionals and commit `873c8bcd` to Lead System Architect (`gpt-6.1-sol`).\\n39:- Remote dart compile and tests verified on Shiva clone: `bb build:yin-repl-peer` (rc=0), `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure.stream-eval-test` (13/13 passed).\\n43:- Architect: gpt-6.1-sol | Prompt: collab/yang-clojure/1793950384477-architect-dart-cljd-guards-review.prompt.md | Thread: 01a1afc6-bb16-7490-b918-260aa3588fe9\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1793950384477-architect-dart-cljd-guards-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'python3 -B .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target 873c8bcd''^..873c8bcd; sed -n '\\\"'1,100p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; sed -n '1,95p' test/yang/clojure/stream_eval_test.cljc; sed -n '1,80p' test/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"python3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-GgfLhCYx' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-11-06 14:34:33.196 xcodebuild[8560:112150070]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-11-06 14:34:33.425 xcodebuild[8560:112150068] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-7YCDx0Gu' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-11-06 14:34:34.163 xcodebuild[8564:112150091]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-11-06 14:34:34.354 xcodebuild[8564:112150089] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\n# Code Review Summary for `873c8bcd^..873c8bcd`\\n\\n## Executive Overview\\n- **Total Files Changed:** 3\\n- **Lines Added:** +12 | **Lines Deleted:** -8\\n- **Test-to-Source Additions Ratio:** 0.0 (0 test lines vs 12 source lines)\\n- **Overall Change Risk:** `LOW`\\n\\n### Included Commits\\n- 873c8bcd fix(dart): add reader conditionals for ClojureDart compilation\\n\\n## Automated Scan Findings\\n✅ No critical security or code quality smells detected by automated scan.\\n\\n## File Churn & Risk Breakdown\\n| File Path | Category | +Add | -Del | Risk |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | Source Code | +9 | -7 | `Medium` |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` | Source Code | +2 | -1 | `Medium` |\\n| `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc` | Source Code | +1 | -0 | `Medium` |\\n\\n## Reviewer Focus & Recommendations\\n---\\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\\n---\\n\\n# BUILD & TEST\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n```sh\\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \\\"name\\\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \\\"Remote test servers\\\" below for\\n# which lanes may overlap.\\n#\\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01.\\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\\n# overlap lanes, see \\\"Remote test servers\\\" below).\\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\\n\\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\\n```\\n\\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\\n\\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\\n(ns yang.clojure.stream-eval-test\\n  \\\"yang.clojure stream programs on yin.vm, evaluated through the yin.repl\\n   shell, which is the composition around dao.stream media: each program\\n   is compiled by yang.clojure, appended to the program medium as one row\\n   batch, expanded onto the row medium, loaded and run by the evaluator's\\n   observer, and answered on the output medium as printed chunks followed\\n   by one result token (yin.repl; docs/design/dao.stream.md).  The streams\\n   a program makes -- `stream/make`, `put!`, `cursor`, `next!`, `close!`\\n   -- are ring buffers the shell hands the VM as `:make-stream`, so every\\n   stream a program touches is a dao.stream medium.\\n\\n   Every case runs on the four evaluators the shell composes, with the\\n   value texts pinned, so the cases double as a cross-VM parity corpus.\\\"\\n  (:require [dao.test-slow :as slow] [clojure.string :as str]\\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Harness\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(def vm-types\\n  \\\"Every evaluator the shell composes (`yin.repl/vm-constructors`).\\\"\\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\\n\\n\\n(defn- session\\n  \\\"A fresh shell on `vm-type`, optionally around a caller-owned output\\n   medium.\\\"\\n  ([vm-type] (session vm-type nil))\\n  ([vm-type output]\\n   (repl.frontends/create-state (cond-> {:vm-type vm-type}\\n                                  output (assoc :output-stream output)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- evaluate\\n  \\\"Evaluate `lines` in order against one threaded state; `[state texts]`.\\n   The shell is synchronous, so no driver is needed.  The program media are\\n   shared by every state threaded from one session, so a state is never\\n   evaluated against twice.\\\"\\n  [state lines]\\n  (reduce (fn [[state texts] line]\\n            (let [[state' text] (repl/eval-input state line)]\\n              [state' (conj texts text)]))\\n          [state []]\\n          lines))\\n\\n\\n(defn- texts\\n  [vm-type lines]\\n  (second (evaluate (session vm-type) lines)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- ring-handle\\n  [capacity]\\n  (:dao.stream/handle\\n    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\\n                   ring/capacity-key capacity})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- read-all\\n  \\\"Every element on `handle` from its oldest, then `[:end outcome]` for\\n   the outcome that ended the read.\\\"\\n  [handle]\\n  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\\n                  (stream/cursor handle :dao.stream/oldest))\\n         elements []]\\n    (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\\n      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\n        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result)\\n               (conj elements (:dao.stream/value result)))\\n        (conj elements [:end (:dao.stream/outcome result)])))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- stream-ref?\\n  \\\"A rendered stream reference; hosts print map keys in their own order.\\\"\\n  [text]\\n  (and (str/starts-with? text \\\"{\\\")\\n       (str/includes? text \\\":type :stream-ref\\\")))\\n\\n\\n(defn- error?\\n  [text]\\n  (str/starts-with? text \\\"Error: \\\"))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Pure expressions and let bindings\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(def pure-corpus\\n(ns yin.repl.frontend-catalog-test\\n  \\\"The REPL compiles through the frontend catalog its composition supplies\\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.5.6, slice F2): a toy frontend\\n   defined here evaluates on every VM, a session pins its catalog snapshot,\\n   and an id the catalog cannot answer is an unavailable-parser diagnostic\\n   with no fallback.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [clojure.string :as str]\\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\\n    [yin.repl :as repl]\\n    [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- manifest\\n  [revision]\\n  {:yang.frontend/id :example.toy/frontend,\\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\\n   :yang.frontend/revision revision,\\n   :yang.frontend/language :toy,\\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \\\"grammar-address\\\",\\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \\\"program\\\"},\\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema \\\"options-address\\\",\\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile \\\"lowering-address\\\",\\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile \\\"runtime-address\\\",\\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile \\\"support-address\\\"})\\n\\n\\n(defn- toy-binding\\n  \\\"A toy language: a source's value is its length times `scale`.\\\"\\n  [scale]\\n  {:parse count,\\n   :lower (fn [n] (yang.clojure/compile (* scale n)))})\\n\\n\\n(defn- toy-catalog\\n  [revision scale]\\n  (frontend/install (repl.frontends/standard)\\n                    (manifest revision)\\n                    (toy-binding scale)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run\\n  [state line]\\n  (repl/eval-input state line))\\n\\n\\n(deftest a-toy-frontend-evaluates-on-every-vm-test\\n  (let [catalog (toy-catalog \\\"r1\\\" 1)]\\n    (doseq [vm-type (keys repl/vm-constructors)]\\n      (testing (str vm-type)\\n        (let [state (repl/create-state {:frontends catalog,\\n                                        :vm-type vm-type})\\n              [state' switched] (run state \\\"(lang :example.toy/frontend)\\\")\\n              [_ refused] (run state \\\"(lang :toy)\\\")\\n              [_ result] (run state' \\\"abcd\\\")]\\n          (is (= \\\"Switched to :example.toy/frontend\\\" switched))\\n          (is (str/includes? refused \\\"unavailable-parser\\\")\\n              \\\"a language keyword is not a selector\\\")\\n          (is (= \\\"4\\\" result)))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest the-standard-languages-select-by-id-test\\n  (let [state (repl.frontends/create-state)\\n        [python switched] (run state \\\"(lang :yang/python)\\\")\\n        [_ value] (run python \\\"1 + 2\\\")]\\n    (is (= \\\"Switched to :yang/python\\\" switched))\\n    (is (= \\\"3\\\" value))\\n    #?(:clj (is (= \\\"3\\\" (second (run (first (run (repl.frontends/create-state)\\n                                                \\\"(lang :yang/php)\\\"))\\n                                    \\\"<?php echo 1 + 2;\\\")))))\\n    (testing \\\"a language keyword is not a selector\\\"\\n      (let [[_ refused] (run state \\\"(lang :python)\\\")]\\n        (is (str/includes? refused \\\"unavailable-parser\\\")))\\n      (testing \\\"the frontend renders the ANTLR Python repr\\\"\\n        (is (= \\\"'ab'\\\" (second (run python \\\"'a' + 'b'\\\"))))))))\\n\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1793950384477-architect-dart-cljd-guards-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,45p' /Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/sonwh98/clojuredart/7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31/clj/src/cljd/compiler.cljc; sed -n '3535,3645p' /Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/sonwh98/clojuredart/7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31/clj/src/cljd/compiler.cljc; sed -n '4900,4980p' /Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/sonwh98/clojuredart/7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31/clj/src/cljd/compiler.cljc; sed -n '1,90p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; sed -n '1,65p' orchestrator-logs/1793947104-agy-gemini-3.8-flash-yang-clojure-seat-takeover.md; ls .cpcache | head\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\";   Copyright (c) Baptiste Dupuch & Christophe Grand. All rights reserved.\\n;   The use and distribution terms for this software are covered by the\\n;   Eclipse Public License 1.0 (http://opensource.org/licenses/eclipse-1.0.php)\\n;   which can be found in the file epl-v10.html at the root of this distribution.\\n;   By using this software in any fashion, you are agreeing to be bound by\\n;   the terms of this license.\\n;   You must not remove this notice, or any other, from this software.\\n\\n(ns cljd.compiler\\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [macroexpand macroexpand-1 munge compile read])\\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\\n            [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]))\\n\\n(defmacro ^:private imply=> [a b] `(or (not ~a) ~b))\\n\\n(defmacro ^:private equiv<=> [a b] `(let [a# ~a b# ~b] (if a# b# (not b#))))\\n\\n(defmacro ^:private blaming [msg & body]\\n  `(try\\n     ~@body\\n     (catch Exception e#\\n       (throw (ex-info ~msg {} e#)))))\\n\\n(defmacro ^:private warp->> [& forms]\\n  `(->> ~@(reverse forms)))\\n\\n(defn- nat-cmp\\n  \\\"Compare two nameds with runs of [0-9]+\\\"\\n  [a b]\\n  (warp->>\\n    (let [a (name a) b (name b)])\\n    (loop [i 0 j 0 na 0 nb 0])\\n    (let [da (if (< i (.length a)) (long (.charAt a i)) -1)])\\n    (if (<= 48 da 57) (recur (inc i) j (+ da -48 (* 10 na)) nb))\\n    (let [db (if (< j (.length b)) (long (.charAt b j)) -1)])\\n    (if (<= 48 db 57) (recur i (inc j) na (+ db -48 (* 10 nb))))\\n    (if (not= na nb) (- na nb))\\n    (if (not= da db) (- da db))\\n    (if (= -1 da) 0)\\n    (recur (inc i) (inc j) 0 0)))\\n\\n(defn read [opts in]\\n  (cljd.lang.LispReader/read in opts))\\n\\n        exclude (into (set exclude) (keys rename))\\n        include (if only (set only) any?)\\n        refer (for [{:keys [type name] {:keys [private]} :meta} (vals (@nses 'cljd.core))\\n                    :when (and (= :field type) (not private)\\n                            (include name) (not (exclude name)))]\\n                name)]\\n    ['cljd.core\\n     :refer refer\\n     :rename (or rename {})]))\\n\\n(defn emit-ns [[_ ns-sym & ns-clauses :as ns-form] _]\\n  (when (or (not *hosted*) *host-eval*)\\n    (let [[ns-meta ns-clauses] (split-with #(or (string? %) (map? %)) ns-clauses)\\n          ns-meta (into {} (map #(if (string? %) [:doc %] %)) ns-meta)\\n          refer-clojures (if (= 'cljd.core ns-sym)\\n                           [[:refer-clojure :only []]]\\n                           (or (seq (filter #(= :refer-clojure (first %)) ns-clauses)) [[:refer-clojure]]))\\n          host-ns-directives (some #(when (= :host-ns (first %)) (next %)) ns-clauses)\\n          require-specs\\n          (->>\\n            (concat\\n              (map refer-clojure-to-require refer-clojures)\\n              (for [[directive & specs :as clause] ns-clauses\\n                    :when clause ; allow nils produced by conditionals\\n                    :let [f (case directive\\n                              :require #(if (sequential? %) % [%])\\n                              :import import-to-require\\n                              :use use-to-require\\n                              (:refer-clojure :host-ns) nil)]\\n                    :when f\\n                    spec specs\\n                    ; allow nils produced by conditionals\\n                    :when spec]\\n                (f spec)))\\n            (map (fn [[lib & more :as spec]]\\n                   (or (some-> (cljdize lib) (cons more))\\n                     spec))))\\n          ns-lib (ns-to-lib ns-sym)\\n          ns-map (-> ns-prototype\\n                   (assoc :meta ns-meta)\\n                   (assoc :lib ns-lib)\\n                   (assoc-in [:imports ns-lib] {:clj-alias (name ns-sym)}))\\n          ns-map\\n          (reduce #(%2 %1) ns-map\\n            (for [[lib & {:keys [as refer rename as-alias]}] require-specs\\n                  :let [_ (when (and (string? lib) (nil? (analyzer-info lib)))\\n                            (throw (Exception. (str \\\"Can't find Dart lib: \\\" lib))))\\n                        _ (when-not (or (nil? refer) (and (coll? refer) (every? symbol? refer)))\\n                            (throw (ex-info \\\":refer expects a collection of symbols; :refer :all is not supported.\\\" {:refer refer})))\\n                        clj-ns (when-not (string? lib) lib)\\n                        alias-only (and as-alias (not (or as refer rename)))\\n                        dartlib (warp->>\\n                                  (if (string? lib) lib)\\n                                  (if-some [{:keys [lib]} (@nses lib)] lib)\\n                                  (if (= ns-sym lib) ns-lib)\\n                                  (if alias-only (stub-alias-namespace lib))\\n                                  (compile-namespace lib))\\n                        dart-alias (global-lib-alias dartlib clj-ns)\\n                        clj-alias (name (or as as-alias clj-ns (str \\\"lib:\\\" dart-alias)))\\n                        to-dart-sym (if clj-ns #(munge % {}) identity)]]\\n              (fn [ns-map]\\n                (-> ns-map\\n                  (cond-> (and (not alias-only) (nil? (get (:imports ns-map) dartlib)))\\n                    (assoc-in [:imports dartlib] {:clj-alias clj-alias}))\\n                  (assoc-in [:clj-aliases clj-alias] dartlib)\\n                  (cond-> as-alias (assoc-in [:clj-aliases as-alias] dartlib))\\n                  (update :mappings into\\n                    (let [source (if (string? lib)\\n                                   #(analyzer-info lib (name %))\\n                                   (@nses lib))]\\n                      (for [to refer :let [from (get rename to to)]]\\n                        (if-not (source to)\\n                          (throw (Exception. (str \\\"Can't find \\\" to \\\" in \\\" lib)))\\n                          [from (symbol clj-alias (name to))]))))))))\\n          host-aliases (into #{}\\n                         (for [[op & more] host-ns-directives\\n                               :when (= :require op)\\n                               lib more\\n                               :when (sequential? lib)\\n                               :let [[_ & {:keys [as]}] lib]\\n                               :when as]\\n                           as))\\n          host-ns-directives\\n          (concat\\n            host-ns-directives\\n            (for [[lib & {:keys [refer as] :as options}] require-specs\\n                  :when (not (host-aliases as))\\n                  :let [host-ns (some-> (get @nses lib) :host-ns ns-name)]\\n                  :when (and host-ns (not= ns-sym lib))\\n                  :let [options\\n                        (assoc options :refer\\n                          (into []\\n                            (comp\\n                              (filter (comp :macro-support :meta (@nses 'cljd.core)))\\n                              ; strip metadata otherwise CLJ embeds it in generated\\n                              ; class and you get too large of constant\\n                              (map #(with-meta % nil)))\\n                            refer))]]\\n              (list :require (into [host-ns] cat options))))\\n          ns-map (cond-> ns-map\\n                   *host-eval* (assoc :host-ns (create-host-ns ns-sym host-ns-directives)))]\\n      (global-lib-alias ns-lib ns-sym)\\n      (set! *current-ns* ns-sym)\\n      (swap! nses assoc ns-sym ns-map)))\\n  (when-not *host-eval*\\n    (set! dynamic-warning (if (get-in @nses [ns-sym :meta :no-dynamic])\\n                            on-dynamic-fail\\n                            on-dynamic-warn))))\\n\\n(defn- emit-no-recur [expr env]\\n  (let [dart-expr (emit expr env)]\\n    (let [{:keys [opt-kind fixed-params-types opt-params-types]}\\n          (parse-dart-params-types (map dart-type-params-reader x))]\\n      (when (= :positional opt-kind)\\n        (throw (Exception. (str \\\"A record type can't have optional fields: \\\" (pr-str x)))))\\n      (with-meta 'dart:core/Record {:fields-types {:fixed-fields-types fixed-params-types\\n                                                   :named-fields-types opt-params-types}}))\\n    :else\\n    (throw (Exception. (str \\\"Unsupported type literal syntax: \\\" (pr-str x))))))\\n\\n(def dart-data-readers\\n  {'dart #(tagged-literal 'dart %)\\n   '/ dart-type-params-reader})\\n\\n(def cljd-resolver\\n  (reify #?(:clj cljd.lang.LispReader$Resolver\\n            :cljd cljd.reader/IResolver)\\n    (currentNS [_] *current-ns*)\\n    (resolveClass [_ sym]\\n      (get-in @nses [*current-ns* :mappings sym]))\\n    (resolveAlias [_ sym]\\n      (let [{:keys [libs] :as nses} @nses\\n            {:keys [clj-aliases]} (nses *current-ns*)]\\n        (when-some [lib (some-> sym name clj-aliases libs)]\\n          (or (:ns lib)\\n            (symbol (str \\\"$lib:\\\" (:dart-alias lib)))))))\\n    (resolveVar [_ sym] nil)))\\n\\n(defmacro with-cljd-reader [& body]\\n  `(binding [*data-readers* (into *data-readers* dart-data-readers)\\n             *reader-resolver* cljd-resolver]\\n     ~@body))\\n\\n(defn load-input [in]\\n  #?(:clj\\n     (with-cljd-reader\\n       (let [in (clojure.lang.LineNumberingPushbackReader. in)]\\n         (binding [dynamic-warning on-dynamic-warn]\\n           (loop []\\n             (let [form (read {:eof in :read-cond :allow :features #{:cljd}} in)]\\n               (when-not (identical? form in)\\n                 (try\\n                   (binding [*locals-gen* {}] (emit form {}))\\n                   (catch Exception e\\n                     (throw (if (::emit-stack (ex-data e))\\n                              e\\n                              (ex-info \\\"Compilation error.\\\" {:form form} e)))))\\n                 (recur)))))))))\\n\\n(defn host-load-input [in]\\n  #?(:clj\\n     (with-cljd-reader\\n       (let [in (clojure.lang.LineNumberingPushbackReader. in)]\\n         (binding [dynamic-warning on-dynamic-warn]\\n           (loop []\\n             (let [form (read {:eof in :read-cond :allow\\n                               :features #{:cljd :cljd/clj-host :clj}} in)]\\n               (when-not (identical? form in)\\n                 (binding [*locals-gen* {}] (host-eval form))\\n                 (recur)))))))))\\n\\n(defn- rename-lib [{:keys [libs dart-aliases] :as nses} from to]\\n  (let [{:keys [ns dart-alias] :as m} (libs from)\\n        nses (assoc nses\\n               :libs (-> libs (dissoc from) (assoc to m))\\n               :dart-aliases (assoc dart-aliases dart-alias to))]\\n    (into nses (keep (fn [[ns ns-map]]\\n                       (when (symbol? ns)\\n                         (let [{:keys [clj-aliases imports lib contribs]} ns-map\\n                               imports (-> imports (dissoc from) (assoc to (imports from)))\\n                               clj-aliases (into {}\\n                                             (map (fn [[alias lib]]\\n                                                    [alias (if (= lib from) to lib)]))\\n                                             clj-aliases)\\n                               contribs (if (get contribs from) (-> contribs (dissoc from) (assoc to to)) contribs)]\\n                           [ns (assoc ns-map :lib (if (= lib from) to lib)\\n                                 :imports imports :clj-aliases clj-aliases\\n                                 :contribs contribs)])))) nses)))\\n\\n(defn compile-input [in]\\n  (binding [*host-eval* false]\\n    (load-input in)\\n---\\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\\n---\\n\\n# BUILD & TEST\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n```sh\\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \\\"name\\\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \\\"Remote test servers\\\" below for\\n# which lanes may overlap.\\n#\\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01.\\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\\n# overlap lanes, see \\\"Remote test servers\\\" below).\\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\\n\\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\\n```\\n\\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\\n\\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\\n# Orchestrator Session Log: yang.clojure track takeover\\n\\nPrior session log: `orchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md`\\nHandoff reference: `collab/yang-clojure/1794920000000-orchestrator-handoff-yang-clojure-seat.md`\\n\\n## 2026-11-06 13:38:28 +07 — Seat takeover & track state re-derivation\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-06 06:38:28 GMT\\nCoding-Agent: agy\\nSession-ID: a7ceb056-3aed-4ccc-9f87-9729e472c726\\nTree: master@75d320cf, uncommitted changes: collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.prompt.md\\nDone:\\n- Established Lead Engineering Orchestrator seat for the yang.clojure track.\\n- Re-derived tree and track state from git log, git status, and the filesystem. Verified commit 75d320cf already landed the handoff note (`collab/yang-clojure/1794920000000-orchestrator-handoff-yang-clojure-seat.md`), resolving the previous Xcode license block on git operations.\\n- Confirmed kernel gate status :pass reached on master via merge commit a7dc47c2 (165/165 admitted arities credited).\\n- Re-read orchestrator.md, team.md, routing-status.md, and updated build-n-test.md (including PID-based remote process management from commit 1ea367ee).\\n- Verified signed Addendum A v3 (`collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md`) and the generalization design (`collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`).\\n- Confirmed pending relays in `collab/yang-call/1794650000000` and `collab/jolt/1794660000000` are ready for distribution.\\nDecisions: Follow handoff roadmap: (1) Re-run nightly on remote hosts using exact PID protocol; (2) Dispatch H3-6 audit round to formally close kernel gate; (3) Distribute pending relays; (4) Prepare frontend adoption briefs absorbing ts/php design feedback.\\nVerification:\\n- `which git && git --version && git status`: /usr/bin/git, Apple Git-157, master up to date with origin/master at 75d320cf.\\n- `git diff collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.prompt.md`: continuation addendum from prior seat verified.\\n\\n## 2026-11-06 14:33:06 +07 — Fix ClojureDart compilation break and dispatch Lead System Architect review\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-06 07:33:06 GMT\\nCoding-Agent: agy\\nSession-ID: a7ceb056-3aed-4ccc-9f87-9729e472c726\\nTree: master@873c8bcd, clean\\nDone:\\n- Root-caused Shiva dart nightly failure from `collab/yang-clojure/1793905679000-orchestrator-dart-cljd-compile-break.glm-5.3-flash.findings.md`:\\n  1. ClojureDart matched :clj reader conditional requires in `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`, attempting to load non-existent `cljd.tools.reader` and failing on `rt/string-push-back-reader` in `read-forms`.\\n  2. `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc` used `defquoted` which expands to `edn/read-string` under cljd, but lacked `#?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])`.\\n  3. `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` required JVM Java ANTLR classes for PHP under `#?@(:clj ...)`, which ClojureDart matched without `:cljd []`.\\n- Landed commit `873c8bcd` (`fix(dart): add reader conditionals for ClojureDart compilation`).\\n- Noted and cor\n... 7260935 bytes omitted ...\n� every rule entry, every `getEpsilonTarget` closure step and every consumed token (the unit that sees the `1+` quadratic: prediction's DFA walk does not accept until its statement ends, so every loop decision re-consumes the rest of the statement — 64,024,002 consumptions for a 16,002-token 8,000-operator chain; a counter of closure steps and rule entries alone sees the chain's work linear, measured) — refused as status -7 `work <measured> <bound>` (the same status as the nesting guards, not -8: the message names the axis), `{:diagnostic :parser-budget :axis :work}`; no unit throws inside a full-context prediction (its consume would unwind past the reach computation the leak fix protects); checked again at every prediction's entry and after recognition; a work refusal resets the worker's parser DFA so a refused source refuses on retry; `kMaxWork` 600,000,000, calibrated (`bb calibrate:jolt-j5 --work`, build/j5b/work.edn) from the measured maximum over the whole parsing corpus — the gated 20,000-operator `1+` chain at 400,129,567 units is the floor — with the adversarial curves above it (`1*`x4,000 about 8.1e8, refuses mid-walk; `1+` past 24,491 operators refuses); the corpus, the at-bound nesting shapes, the 4 MiB flat inputs and the gated flat sizes parse unchanged, zero parity pins. Divergences from the row's plan recorded: the 10 s refusal walls were infeasible with the floor the existing gates set (refusing at 600,000,000 units costs the time those units cost — about 20 s for the `1+` family, minutes-becoming-tens-of-seconds for the `1*` walk), and the bound is not per-byte (per-byte cannot separate a 24 KB `1*` chain from a 24 KB legitimate source). The lexer's per-NEWLINE constant (two `std::regex` constructions per newline in the generated lexer base) is linear in work but unbounded in wall: disclosed in §7.6, not bounded. Linux evidence pending (the orchestrator closes this row); precondition for parsing remotely sourced Python (J6) | P2 |\\\\\\\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:350:| yang.clojure: the slice-9 kernel differential gate is honestly blocked at **107/165 credited (39 direct + 68 named integrations), 58 unexercised admitted arities**, 100 agreements, 2 recorded deviations (`elab-after-qed`, `check-after-qed`), 2 blocked fixtures, 2 declared upstream failures; the earlier 145/165-and-20 accounting predated the common-call reconciliation and under-counted (38 named-integration trace paths no longer exist) | hardening-3 H3-0 (the architect's finding: the deviation classifier required a bare closure where the reconciled compiler publishes the admitted §8.10 descriptor) | yang.clojure | H3-0 repaired the bookkeeping (versioned slice9_declarations.edn drives a representation-aware classifier with declared-call, message and script revalidation; the writer carries declared dispositions; a writer round-trip test replays the checked-in evidence) — repair, not closure; H3-1..H3-5 close the 58 per the approved hardening-3 plan | P2 |\\\\\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:397:## 2026-10-29 19:5x +0700 — the session-id collision lesson logged; the cross-language demo and the 8.10 spec distinction recorded\\\\\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:400:Done: The owner asked two questions that produced recorded findings: (1) why no terminals are visible (the delegates run as background processes writing to collab/ logs, not interactive terminals; the shiva lanes run in tmux on the remote server), and (2) whether the section 8.10 cross-language calling convention spec is unnecessary given that cross-language calls already work. The answer to (2): no — the demo proved the mechanism (the substrate routes calls correctly), but the spec defines the semantics (null sentinels, number kinds, opaque handles, references, exceptions, cleanup, ownership). The calls work at the engine level; the contract for what values mean at the boundary didn't exist until the spec defined it. The distinction: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the pipe works\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"what flows through the pipe and what happens when it leaks.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:402:Verification: the cross-language demo (test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj, landed 2e1d09e6) proves the mechanism; the section 8.10 spec defines the semantics.\\\\\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:646:Decisions: the handoff artifact is this log entry — the yang.call API surface (entry, eligible?, invocation, invocation-with, valid-invocation?, condition, thrown, transfer, invoke, invoke-with), the dependency addresses (yang.core.call, yang.core.uast, yang.core.prelude, yin.vm, yin.vm.module), and the convention spec (yang.antlr.md section 8.10, committed eb8030e8, kimi-approved).\\\\\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:685:Done: (1) The peer python-orchestrator note (collab/1793610000000-...) claimed the section 8.10.11 gap for TS/PHP; codex verified it READ-ONLY (collab/orch-lane/1793630000000-engineer-crosslang-gap-verify.gpt-6-luna.stdout.log): PARTIAL — the rewrites (cross_lang_test.clj:110-137 postwalk) and synthetic cells (call_test.cljc:202-260 inline fns) CONFIRMED with line evidence; the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"bypass\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" framing too broad (the calls already route through invoke-with/:yang.call/entry); no qualifying real-source x convention test for TS/PHP anywhere. (2) The TS S11 round landed (cccebf3e on yang-ts-t3, PUSHED and shiva-verified: JVM subsystem 18 ns / 103 tests / 0 failures in the fresh ts3b clone): direct TS->PHP source calls pass on JVM and Node; the higher-order callback leg was blocked because PHP's resolver rejected TS cells. (3) The PHP conformance round landed (d145085b: unchanged PHP source calling a named TS export + the stored-called-returned closure leg; PHP closures publish a yang.call entry on the closure value) and the foreign-admission round landed (edc50134: PHP admits conforming foreign callable cells through the shared resolver; non-conforming cells keep the undefined-function diagnostic; the PHP-side callback identity test passes). Both PUSHED. (4) The foreach_016 defect fixed (3321ecee: by-ref foreach cursor preserved across array_unshift reindexing; the pin matched on all four VMs at 481 ms). (5) The e2e red triaged by reproduction at the tip: the 115/271 PHPT selection mismatches are the LONG-STANDING S10 backlog (foreach by-ref, gc, unset CV, named-params families); the refusals-are-named FOO diagnostic regression is REAL (echo FOO produces nil instead of :yang.php/unsupported/:constant — likely the P6 constants work); plus one error. The triage round (manifest bookkeeping for the selection, the FOO fix, the error, the gc_013 disposition) dispatched to luna. (6) gc_013 oracle cross-check run by the seat on shiva (docker php:8.3-cli, the pinned source): real PHP outputs bool(true)/ok — the PIN IS CORRECT; the mismatch is the engine's cycle-collection semantics -> a named known-gap row. (7) The lane lessons: the codex resume writer-lock recursed (the r2 nuance dispatch failed with thread-store conflict; sol's r1 had already converged correctly, so no re-dispatch needed); scratch-clone focused runs need clojure -M:test; the -e :slow flag EXCLUDES slow tests (lane7 forgot it and ran the 259 s gc_013 stress case); an orphaned 100%-CPU test-runner survived a tmux kill-session and burned 2.5 h before the seat killed it.\\\\\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:729:Next: the P7-a execution-budget round (kimi's ruled contract, now unblocked by the matrix); the P4 S9-S12 and P6 S6+ plan steps; the route-status of remaining §8.10.11 evidence (the higher-order legs for ts<->php exist inside the matrix now).\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:2956:Done: Chartered and drove the code-as-tuples design unit per the owner's seven rulings. Author claude-fable-5.1 (fresh session 8677b374, then resumed for revision), reviewer gpt-6-astra (codex thread 01a09fcc), independence preserved (Claude↔GPT), orchestrator verified all rounds' surprising claims against source (100% held). Round 1 draft: docs/design/yin.vm.tuples.md 780 lines — three-layer stance (objects/refs/projection), full AST grammar table, boundary calls (:vm/store-update excluded; :stream/close kept with walker gaining the arm), whole-tree addressing, querying, VM load paths, ledger-as-refs, honest migration + blockers. Round 1 review: REJECT, 12 P1s, convergent (central decision, grammar inventory, boundary calls, addressing, query mechanics, migration counts all verified sound; defects all integration-protocol: keyword store keys vs sym kind, ledger rows illegal under local-datom?, runtime bookkeeping written into the AST node under :frame, dependency queries missing parked ids, occurrence identity, macro admission, lowering revision, encoder blocker scope). Round 2 revision: all 12 addressed, none overruled, 780→1132 lines — frame schema table (§2.6), ledger records as content-addressed objects entering as local event entities (§8.1-8.2, legal under local-datom?/pad-datom, no reserved-id allocation), occurrence keys [root-address path], macro declaration carriage (§8.5), stamped derivation records, shared validator + UCF §7.3.4 projection-primary supersession. Round 2 re-review (after a codex usage-limit abort at ~21:45, auto-retried 00:12 via one-shot cron after reset): REJECT again — 5/12 resolved (frames, shared validator, ledger legality, reserved ops, as-of — as-of executed and passed), 1 regressed (encoder gate: the revision's \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"reject lists\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" restricted domain is itself unsound — (seq [1 2]) and metadata-carrying vectors still collide), 6 narrowed-not-resolved (store-key domain must be the full admitted data domain; plain-data result condition still admits effect descriptors since effect? = any map with :effect; dependency completion still uses any-environment satisfaction; occurrence identity lacks source/batch and expansion-event qualification; macro carriage lacks whole-batch admission/disconnected definitions/stray-mark rejection; derivation stamp must pin the lowering algorithm, not reuse UCF's execution-contract stamp; segment effect query returns mnemonics vs the :stream/put vocabulary). Central representation decisions again endorsed: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sound\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"closer to implementable\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8483:medium), F2 (yang.antlr.md §8.1 contradiction), F3 (completion/encoder must refuse :cell-ref in slice 1), F4-F7 low/doc.\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8485:Decisions: none taken; owner decisions pending (copy-on-lift, naming cell vs box, amend §8.1, F1 scheduling, accept\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:8503:D3 amend yang.antlr.md §8.1 to a task-owned cell heap (state threading allowed per frontend); D4 F1 fix before cell\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:9271:  8.5.1/8.11/9.3/11/12 amendments and the corrected RecursionError line. Everything pending-labelled; git grep\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:10881:      - Documentation: Updated `docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md` (§4.1, §4.2, §6.3, §6.4, §8.1) and `docs/design/yang.antlr.md` (§8.5.6).\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11109:  - Phase 3 brief: linearizer (`project` per §3.3), loader rules (§3.4, both load paths), static analysis (§8.1 def/use/L/saved), with an independent liveness reference implementation; gates per §10.\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11113:## 2026-10-10 18:10:00 +07 — semantic-register-vm phase 3 landed (linearizer, §3.4 validator, §8.1 liveness); G3 green\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:12001:  loss recorded (Python cannot call same-session Clojure macros until the §8.