imits pinned as documented expectations - the empirical evidence slice for the section 8.10 story discussed with the owner this session. Operational note recorded: a trailing & inside a backgrounded dispatch DETACHES the child (it survives; the wrapper completes empty) - the failure mode differs from a kill; check process liveness and log growth before re-dispatching, and never re-dispatch under a live session id (the collision error is the tell).\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13855:Decisions: the number-kinds correction propagates to the future 8.10 ABI work: the portable-value tier is narrower than assumed (booleans/strings TBD; numbers need a conversion rule or bigint acceptance).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:158:(§8.1), as a foreign engine's layout is, and does not enter A.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:223:where `L(p)` is the standard live-in set at the resume pc `p` (§8.1),\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:557:   liveness of §8.1 is computed over the real successor relation, in\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:724:`saved(pc, rd)` from A (§8.1) and refuses a window with a register\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:778:from A (§8.1), and keeps `:yin.safepoint/layout` as a map from physical\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:838:checksum are regenerated then, mechanically (derivations design §8.1-8.2).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:863:### 8.1 Static facts per pc: def, use, live\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:928:     windows are `saved(p, rd)` at *reachable* safepoints (§8.1), and\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:949:     operands (step 3) and every saved window come from §8.1's\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:965:   virtual live-out over the instruction's **actual successors** (§8.1)\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1024:at the slice and once at cutover (derivations design §8.1); nothing is\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1061:descriptors lose their lift declaration (derivations design §8.1-8.2);\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1084:   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg --files collab | rg '1794600000000|attribution|addendum'; cat docs/agents/routing-status.md; cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg --files collab | rg '1794600000000|attribution|addendum'; cat docs/agents/routing-status.md; cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.glm-5.3.stdout.log\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794610000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.qwen-review.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.astra-review.stdout.log\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a.astra-review.stdout.log\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794620000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.kimi-review.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-DRAFT.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.prompt.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1794600000000-engineer-roundA-p1-fixes.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log\\\\\\\\ncollab/yang-python/1793410000000-orchestrator-yang-python-attribution-note.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/dao-jing/1790012238375-architect-jing-cbor-eve-addendum.prompt.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/yin-vm/1790016536012-architect-debruijn-vm-revision-r4-addendum.prompt.md\\\\\\\\ncollab/yin-vm/1791990000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase5c-r2.mutant-addendum.md\\\\\\\\n# Delegate routing status\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDurable record of owner-relayed delegate CLI/model availability and budget\\\\\\\\nstatus. No tool exposes this automatically (weekly quotas, provider outages,\\\\\\\\nspending caps) — the owner relays it in conversation, and it otherwise dies\\\\\\\\nwith that session. This file is what lets a different orchestrator seat, in a\\\\\\\\nfresh session with no shared history, know the current routing constraints\\\\\\\\nwithout re-asking or discovering them the hard way.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAppend-only in spirit, like `docs/orchestrator-log.md`: when a status goes\\\\\\\\nstale or is superseded, add a new entry rather than editing the old one, so\\\\\\\\nthe history of what was true when stays visible. Unlike the work log, this\\\\\\\\nfile may be edited to trim entries that are long superseded and no longer\\\\\\\\nuseful context, since this is a status board, not a provenance record.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEvery entry states: the destination, what the owner said, when, and how to\\\\\\\\napply it. Treat every entry here as a claim to re-verify (a quota resets, an\\\\\\\\noutage resolves), not as permanent authority — the same posture as the work\\\\\\\\nlog.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## How to apply\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBefore routing a new dispatch to any metered/quota-based destination, check\\\\\\\\nthis file's most recent entry for that destination. If none exists or the\\\\\\\\nstated reset time has passed, the status is unknown — proceed normally, but\\\\\\\\nconsider a cheap sanity check (a trivial prompt) before committing a\\\\\\\\nreal task to a destination that failed recently. When the owner relays a new\\\\\\\\nstatus in conversation, add an entry here before continuing, so it survives\\\\\\\\npast the current session.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Current status\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 measured — qwen-code LIVE: Alibaba's `qwen` CLI configured on the Token Plan and verified\\\\\\\\nDistinct from the withdrawn claude-wrapper of this morning: `qwen` now means `@qwen-code/qwen-code@0.17.0` (nvm node v26.1.0 npm-global; a second mise install was found and removed today at the owner's request). The owner's key `sk-sp-H.LXYLM.f0Vo.…` is registered in ~/.qwen/settings.json env; the gateway is https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1 (region-bound: the key 403s at cn-beijing). Measured usable catalog: qwen3.8-max / qwen3.8-flash / qwen3.7-max / qwen3.6-flash / deepseek-v4-pro — everything else the pre-existing auto-written config listed is \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Access to model denied\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Model not exist\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Headless probe `qwen -p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" < /dev/null` returned OK rc=0. Session-ID mechanics not yet measured; do not invent them. Consequence: qwen is an available implementation destination NOW; parallel capacity qwen | kimi | glm | muse | codex. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (qwen3.8-flash).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 measured then withdrawn — the `qwen` wrapper lane is REMOVED (name collision with Alibaba's `qwen-code` agent)\\\\\\\\nThe Model Studio Token Plan measurement stands (registered via `bl auth login --config token-plan`; Token Plan Anthropic endpoint https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/apps/anthropic works end-to-end through a claude-family wrapper; measured catalog qwen3.8-max + qwen3.8-flash only; cn-beijing gateway 403s this key; `bl config agent --agent claude-code` is a global takeover — CAUTION stands). But the `~/.local/bin/qwen` wrapper was deleted the same day: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"qwen\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" collides with Alibaba's separate `qwen-code` coding agent, making the name ambiguous as a delegate. NO qwen dispatch lane is installed; re-create one under a non-colliding name before routing anything here. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 owner request — measured: muse-spark-1.3 WORKS on the API-key lane (contributor mode on)\\\\\\\\nProbe on the laptop: `muse exec --trust-workspace --approval-mode never --model muse-spark-1.3` returned OK rc=0 in a fresh trusted dir. `muse usage` reports \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No subscription allowance (api_key)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" — the run is billed through the persisted API key (~/.config/muse/api-key, keychain auth), not the subscription window. Contributor mode is globally enabled in settings.json. Owner follow-up measured: the explicit ID `--model muse-spark-1.3-contributor` ALSO works (OK rc=0, same recipe) — so both the plain alias with contributor mode inherited from settings and the explicit `-contributor` suffix are valid dispatch forms; the earlier note that \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"contributor is only the mode, not part of the model ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" was wrong. Consequence: spark-1.3 API dispatches are live regardless of the subscription window state; wonder-1.0 remains the subscription-lane model. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 owner relay — codex is available again\\\\\\\\nOwner relay: codex may be dispatched; the 06:10 relay's \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no new codex dispatches\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" line is lifted. Route codex rounds per team.md and delegate-invocation-reference.md as usual. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 07:5x +07 — measured: muse headless root-caused on shiva; the recipe works on BOTH servers now\\\\\\\\nThe two shiva failure modes are now reproduced and fixed (entered in delegate-invocation-reference.md): (1) headless `muse exec` without `--trust-workspace` runs UNTRUSTED in any root not in ~/.config/muse/trust.json (only /home/sto/workspace/datomworld is listed server-side) — agent delegation silently off; a trivial probe still passes, so probe-only checks masked it; (2) the default --approval-mode on-request blocks forever headless with no API traffic — measured: a tool-using round hung to SIGTERM at 180s having done zero work. With `--trust-workspace --approval-mode never` a tool-using round completes in seconds; the sandbox (bwrap + user namespaces, both present on shiva AND jupiter) stays ON and the Bubblewrap banner is informational. Verified end-to-end on shiva and jupiter (muse 1.4.14, muse-wonder-1.0): headless muse work rounds are live on both servers. The 04:0x \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"muse wedges silently on shiva\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" entry is explained by mechanism (2), not an API outage. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 06:10 +07 — owner relay: muse, agy, glm, kimi are the only cli tools available\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 03:10 +07 — measured: muse subscription window LIVE again (the 06:10 relay's muse lane is open)\\\\\\\\nProbe: `muse exec --model muse-wonder-1.0` with a fresh caller UUID returned \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OK\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (rc=0) at 03:10 +07 — earlier than the 20:41 window estimate recorded on 11-02; the reset must have been the daily window, not the 24h one. Consequence: muse is the default implementation destination NOW (with the standing kimi code-quality gate); agy stays out until its quota reset (~7 days from the 11-02 exhaustion). No new codex or mistral dispatches (the 06:10 relay). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 03:2x +0700 — correction: agy is LIVE on both hosts (the earlier \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"quota\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" read was a per-session limit, not account exhaustion)\\\\\\\\nOwner challenged the agy-quota assumption. Measured: fresh `agy --model gemini-4-argon-high` probes return OK on the laptop and on shiva (rc=0, real responses). The 11-02 cljd round died with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Individual quota reached, resets in 165h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" — that was the SESSION/turn budget of one 6,600-second 645k-token turn, not the account. Lesson (same class as the muse reset misread): a delegate CLI's own reset estimate is not availability; always probe with a fresh cheap session before ruling a destination out. agy is a live implementation destination NOW (with the standing kimi quality gate); the long-round budget stays a real constraint — split big rounds into resumed sessions rather than one turn. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 03:4x +0700 — amendment to the 03:2x correction: agy IS quota-limited after all (intermittent)\\\\\\\\nThe fresh-session probes passed at 03:1x-03:2x, but the dispatched real work round (xlang slice 1 on shiva) died instantly with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Individual quota reached, resets in ~161h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", and an immediate laptop probe also returns quota-reached. True shape: the account pool is at its individual ceiling; small probes occasionally squeak through but a real work round cannot complete. AGY: unusable for work rounds until the reset (~161h); the probes' success was the tail of the pool, not availability. Implementation falls back to muse (live) for work rounds; kimi gate unchanged. The seat reverts the 03:2x \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"live on both hosts\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" conclusion to: live-for-probes, quota-walled-for-work. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 0x:xx +0700 — agy model-level routing (argon walled; claude/flash live); muse-on-shiva WORKS headless with --trust-workspace\\\\\\\\nOwner: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"argon has reached quota but gemini-3.8-flash is available and so are agy's claude models.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" Measured: claude-opus-5-5-high and gemini-3.8-flash-high probes return real responses; argon quota-walled (~161h). Implementation rounds route to agy claude-opus-5-5-high (hard rounds) / gemini-3.8-flash-high (light rounds); kimi quality gate unchanged. Separately measured: muse's Linux sandbox needs Bubblewrap user namespaces shiva cannot create — muse dispatched to a shiva worktree printed the sandbox warning and produced no work in 40 min. Muse on shiva: the earlier \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cannot sandbox\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" read was WRONG — the Bubblewrap line is informational; the real gap was the missing --trust-workspace flag in my headless muse exec invocation (interactive muse in the repo trusts on its own; the owner verified both). Headless muse on shiva: `muse exec --trust-workspace --model muse-wonder-1.0 ...`. The reference recipe gains --trust-workspace for non-laptop roots. The xlang slice 1 round re-dispatched from muse to agy claude-opus-5-5-high on shiva. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 04:0x +0700 — agy quota is PER-MODEL: argon ~161h, claude-opus-5-5 ~4h, gemini-3.8-flash fresh; muse headless on shiva wedges silently\\\\\\\\nMeasured: the opus-5-5 finish-round dispatch died instantly with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Individual quota reached, resets in 3h58m24s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" — a per-model window far shorter than argon's 161h. gemini-3.8-flash-high accepted a real round immediately after. Routing: agy models are individually probe-gated before dispatch (cheap probe per model, not per CLI); record each model's window as measured. Separately: the muse headless round on shiva made one burst of edits (good quality — the xlang conformance helper design + rebuilt cross_lang_test) then went silent 55 min with NO API usage on the owner's dev console; killed. Muse-on-shiva headless remains unreliable for work rounds (works interactively per the owner) — work rounds on shiva go to agy; muse work rounds stay on the laptop. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 08:1x +0700 — BLE-track seat: claude billing-walled; codex dispatch made against the 06:10 relay (violation recorded, no further codex)\\\\\\\\nMeasured this session: the `claude` CLI (flat Pro Max lane) now hard-fails with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"can't use your Claude subscription, usually because a payment is past due\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" — treat claude as DOWN until the owner relays otherwise (the wrapper's own message names billing; per this file's rules that is a claim to re-verify, not permanent authority). Separately: this seat dispatched an r5 review to codex gpt-6.1-sol DESPITE the 06:10 owner relay (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no new codex dispatches\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") because it skipped checking this file before routing — the dispatch completed with a real verdict, which does not excuse the violation; recorded per the artifact protocol, and the verdict's findings are being reconciled regardless of the routing defect. Review confirmation rounds for the BLE track resume on allowed destinations only (muse / agy per-model-probe-gated / kimi gate), family-independent from the GLM-family implementer seat. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 15:55 +07 — owner relay: codex is available now\\\\\\\\nSupersedes the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"codex CLOSED until further notice\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" entries (23:45 +07 Nov 2 and the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"codex is out\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" note). Codex is back on the board. The model split from the argon/flash ruling stands: agy gemini-3.8-flash implements, argon reserved for hard problems/architectural review, kimi gates every implementation round. Codex is available for architect-review roles and implementation per the team.md policy. Entered by the yin.repl jolt orchestrator seat.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-11-03 16:1x +07 — acknowledged: codex back on the board\\\\\\\\nThe yang.clojure seat read the 15:55 relay. Consequence: the H3-1 wedge diagnostic's next step (instrument encoder/forward-on-stream to locate the exact non-terminating loop) routes to codex engineering — codex did the strongest adversarial work on this track (the H3-0 review rounds) and the probe infrastructure is already on hardening3-h3-1 (8ea857c1) for it to build on. The kimi quality gate and the yin.vm-ruling boundary (no shared-runtime changes without a minimized reproduction) carry over unchanged. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 01:1x +07 — owner relay: kimi at 97.51%, resets 11-29; reroute to codex\\\\\\\\nOwner, verbatim: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kimi is at 97.51% usage and resets 11-29. reroute to codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Apply: kimi is quota-walled until 2026-11-29 — no new kimi dispatches (the pending gates on this track reroute to codex architect-review roles, which the 15:55 relay restored). The standing kimi quality gate moves to codex reviews for the duration; probe codex cheaply before each dispatch per the file's own rule. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — owner ruling: muse-1.3-contrib implements, gpt-6.1-sol is the architect\\\\\\\\nOwner, verbatim: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"you're the orchestrator.md for this track. use muse-1.3-contrib to implement and gpt-6.1-sol as architect.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Apply: (1) implementation rounds on this track (yang.typescript / yang.php) route to muse model muse-1.3-contrib; (2) architect/design/review rounds route to codex gpt-6.1-sol (per the 15:55 Nov 3 relay, codex is available); (3) the standing muse/mistral quality gate is now sol's review (family-independent: sol reviews muse's work); (4) kimi remains available for architect duty but sol is the named architect for this track; (5) probe muse-1.3-contrib and codex before the first real dispatch per the sanity-check rule. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — measured probes after the owner's muse-1.3-contrib/sol ruling\\\\\\\\ncodex gpt-6.1-sol: LIVE (probe OK, read-only). muse-1.3-contrib: the catalog resolves the id (model-profile show prints a full profile) but muse exec fails twice with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"model muse-1.3-contrib does not exist or you lack access\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (request_ids 49de5c87..., b65cb99b...) — an account access-lane issue, escalated to the owner; implementation dispatches HELD until access is granted or the exact id is confirmed (no silent substitution against the ruling). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — owner: try muse-spark-1.3 — probe OK; implementation lane opens on muse-spark-1.3\\\\\\\\nmuse-1.3-contrib remains access-blocked (two measured exec failures); the owner directed muse-spark-1.3, which probes OK. Implementation rounds on this track now route to muse-spark-1.3 (headless muse exec, laptop, --trust-workspace where needed); gpt-6.1-sol stays the architect/reviewer per the earlier ruling. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — measured: muse-spark-1.3-contrib is ALSO access-blocked; muse-spark-1.3 (plain) is the working lane\\\\\\\\nOwner directed trying muse-spark-1.3-contrib: muse exec fails with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"does not exist or you lack access\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (request_id 88163fe9-713f-4808-8700-cf7cfc5f69ed). The plain muse-spark-1.3 probe returned OK. Implementation lane: muse-spark-1.3. The \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-contrib\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" suffix variants (muse-1.3-contrib, muse-spark-1.3-contrib) both fail on this account — if the owner intends a contrib lane, the account needs its access granted. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — third measured failure on muse-spark-1.3-contrib (owner re-directed the probe)\\\\\\\\nRe-probed at the owner's request: same error, request_id c6cdab06-ebc3-44da-bca0-b52065caf2ed. Both -contrib ids fail on this account; plain muse-spark-1.3 works and carries the implementation lane. If the contrib lane is intended, the account needs the access grant or the exact catalog id from the owner's console. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — the correct contrib id is muse-spark-1.3-contributor; it EXISTS but shares the exhausted quota (resets 2026-11-09)\\\\\\\\nOwner-directed probe: muse-spark-1.3-contributor resolves (no \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"does not exist\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" error — unlike muse-1.3-contrib and muse-spark-1.3-contrib, which are wrong ids) but returns \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"quota exhausted. Your usage window resets at 2026-11-09\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". The whole muse account lane (plain + contributor) is walled until Nov 9. Implementation substitution decision escalated to the owner: kimi-implements + sol-reviews (recommended; kimi landed P7-a/P5/P9/xlang green this session) vs parking implementation until Nov 9. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — owner relays: kimi is OUT of credits; muse-spark-1.3-contributor works now; gpt-6.1-sol is the architect\\\\\\\\nCurrent lanes for this track: IMPLEMENTATION = muse (muse-spark-1.3-contributor); ARCHITECT/REVIEW = codex gpt-6.1-sol (owner-confirmed twice). kimi unavailable (credits) — its architect/gate duty moves to sol. agy remains quota-walled (~Nov 9-10); codex implementation is not used while sol is the named architect (family-independent review preserved: muse implements, sol reviews). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 12:4x +0700 — owner: muse cli is available on shiva — PROBE CONFIRMED (contributor model, rc OK despite bwrap warnings)\\\\\\\\nMeasured: muse exec on shiva with muse-spark-1.3-contributor returns OK. The Linux sandbox still cannot use bwrap (missing --ro-bind-symlink capability; install under writable /home/sto flagged) — muse runs UNSANDBOXED there with warnings, which is acceptable for scratch-clone worktree rounds. Consequence: implementation rounds needing heavy gates (e2e/slow) can run on shiva directly, zero laptop load — the preferred topology under the never-slow-local rule. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 02:5x +0700 — muse work rounds on shiva CONFIRMED unreliable (second sighting): probes succeed, real rounds silently wedge\\\\\\\\npin-fix (2h, zero edits, zero CPU) and p5-record (10 min, same) both alive-but-frozen; shiva load average 0.38 proved it. The 04:35 Nov-3 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"headless unreliable on shiva\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" record stands and now covers muse-spark-1.3-contributor too (the probe OK is a one-shot turn; multi-turn rounds hang on the missing user-namespace sandbox — it runs unsandboxed but wedges). muse work rounds: LAPTOP only (r3 delivered there in ~25 min: commit + honest findings). shiva remains the host for SEAT-run gates (ssh + tmux by this seat). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-11-04 23:4x +07 — owner routing: the cljrt fix r4 goes to glm-5.3\\\\\\\\nAfter two consecutive muse-wonder-1.0 fix rounds failed the cell-ref shape-routing defect (and the final codex gate rejected at d3a35830), the owner instructed \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"delegate it to glm-5.3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" — satisfying the delegate-death rule's diversity condition; the stop is lifted by user instruction. Note: the model name at the process level is `claude --model glm-5.3` (glm is a claude-code-family CLI) — pgrep on 'glm' misses it; check the quirk before judging runs dead (second occurrence of this lesson today). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-05 0x:xx +0700 — cross-track coordination state: cell-ref ruling landed; sweeps dispatched; the xlang matrix's clojure skip CLOSED\\\\\\\\nae91bb8d landed the owner-ruled cell/authentic? policy (yin.vm additive + the shared _descriptor + the yang.clojure sites); the yang.clojure↔TS matrix skip is CLOSED (matrix 13/21/0 on jupiter). This seat: the TS/PHP authenticity sweep round dispatched to muse-spark-1.3-contributor (feat/cellref-sweep, laptop) covering ts typeof :135, ts member-call :1167, and php ~:4229 (verify-first; possibly no code needed there). Smoke-test duty on shiva post-sweep per the reciprocal note. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n2026-11-05 0x:xx +0700 — owner routing update: codex, agy, muse, qwen available; kimi CLI out (kimi via qwen allowed)\\\\\\\\nOwner: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"codex, agy, muse, qwen cli and their models are available. kimi cli is out, but you may use kimi from qwen cli.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" Measured: qwen probe OK (plan mode); implementation form is --approval-mode auto-edit, review form plan (reference lines 429-433). Board: implementation = muse-spark-1.3-contributor (proven) and qwen models (new capacity); architect = gpt-6.1-sol unchanged; agy = quota-walled until ~Nov 9-10; codex = available (sol primarily the architect per the earlier ruling; implementation-capable when the architect lane is idle). Also read: build-n-test.md boundary reconciliation (individual tests local; suite-scale remote only). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Domain Scope\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\\\\\\\\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\\\\\\\\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\\\\\\\\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\\\\\\\\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\\\\\\\\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\\\\\\\\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\\\\\\\\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\\\\\\\\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\\\\\\\\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Core Responsibilities\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\\\\\\\\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\\\\\\\\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\\\\\\\\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Delegation Prompt Template\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```text\\\\\\\\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\\\\\\\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Task: <Task Name>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nImplementers:\\\\\\\\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRead first:\\\\\\\\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\\\\\\\\n- <target-design-file>\\\\\\\\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\\\\\\\\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\\\\\\\\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\\\\\\\\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\\\\\\\\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\\\\\\\\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBegin the final response exactly with:\\\\\\\\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\\\\\\\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\\\\\\\\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n 'astra|Architect|Cost|codex|subscription' docs/agents/team.md; git status --short; git log -3 --oneline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n 'astra|Architect|Cost|codex|subscription' docs/agents/team.md; git status --short; git log -3 --oneline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"25:| [Architect](roles/architect.md)                   | Axioms, invariants, boundaries, architecture                                                           |\\\\\\\\n45:## Available Subscriptions & Cost Constraints\\\\\\\\n47:The Orchestrator routes work using these cost profiles. Flat subscriptions are preferred; metered models are reserved for tasks explicitly requiring them.\\\\\\\\n50:| Provider        | Cost Structure                         | Routing Notes                                                                                               |\\\\\\\\n52:| agy             | Flat: Included                         | Treated as a flat subscription. Use freely within budget.                                                   |\\\\\\\\n54:| qwen            | Token Plan subscription (Alibaba Cloud | The `qwen` CLI is Alibaba's own coding agent (`@qwen-code/qwen-