ructed-descriptor fixture; (P2-1) the direct-apply fallback is value-structural (any entry-less value applies directly), so :yang.call/not-callable is unreachable from source; (P2-2) tail chains through the entry/bridge grow the semantic stack ~9 frames/activation — the slice-4/5 constant-depth invariant was dropped in this diff; (P3s) silent continuation fallback, named-arg errors riding :yang.call/thrown. Escalated (a) the contradiction + (b)-(e) to kimi r4 arbitration (session in collab/1793309600000-*).\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:410:Decisions: P1-2 is an orchestrator-brief vs spec contradiction — my brief's item 5 (hand-constructed fixture) was written by me from the spec's illustrative example, and it conflicts with 8.10.11's remains-data requirement as realized in open Clojure maps; escalated to the section's approving architect rather than resolved by the seat that created the contradiction.\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:1:# Session log — yang.clojure track (hardening + adoption of §8.10 common call)\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:35:Done: glm r3 confirmation (session 3e4d9593, resumed after a plan-only stop): N1 CLOSED (all forged shapes refuse with the qualified :yang.call/not-callable via both operators incl. the def-alias route; admitted + dynamic-eligibility intact both lanes), N2 CLOSED (dao.host.gate-test 14/178; manifests 156/154/155, union 168) — \\\"Ready for Architect sign-off\\\". astra sign-off r1 DENIED on a real P2 the seat had not caught: the invocation admission gate skipped ARGUMENT evaluation on refusal (§8.10.4 requires operands once, left-to-right, before the callee check) — reproduced on both lanes at 12feb7d1 vs abbfb998. Fix round to kimi -> committed 45269e0f (all operands bound before the witness check, both branches reuse the bindings, refused/admitted regressions both lanes). This seat verified 143/1484 