ssion witness — codebase-true shapes, not invented ones); the classifier accepts either representation; the versioned declarations file drives boundary/upstream-value/reason with revalidation guards (declared message == live message, declared script == live script, normalized); negative controls extended (both representations classify; forgeries — missing admission, non-closure entry, wrong type marker, invented shape — refuse; a mutated declaration fails via with-redefs); the writer gained a `dir` overload so the round-trip test exercises the REAL writer against a temp directory replaying the checked-in evidence (no fixture recompute). The muse round's declarations file was retained as-is (kimi had retained it).\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:222:Done: (1) After the owner left the lane question unanswered, the seat implemented H3-0 directly. Reading the pristine harness showed the ENTIRE machinery existed at HEAD — the single root cause was astra's r1 finding: the deviation classifier's `(values/closure? meta)` was representation-stale (the reconciled compiler publishes the admitted §8.10 descriptor at :meta — measured PersistentArrayMap). The vibe rounds had \\\"fixed\\\" everything except this one line's assumption. (2) The seat's implementation: `kernel-callable-descriptor?` (function marker + minted-closure entry + admission witness + true outcomes marker — codebase-true shapes); the classifier accepts both representations; the versioned slice9_declarations.edn (muse round 3's file, kimi-retained) drives boundary/upstream-value/reason with revalidation guards; the declarations contract validated at load (version/provenance/per-fixture exact boundaries/pinned revision — relabeling fails at load); negative controls extended (both representations classify; forgeries, payload/shape mutations, per-lane incompleteness, mutated calls and mutated declarations refuse); the writer gained a dir overload with a real-writer round-tr