ne: glm adoption-S1 review (session e1599324, findings synced to main collab/1793309500000-reviewer-adopt-s1.glm-5.3.findings.md): the A1/A2/A4 mechanics are implemented and probe-verified, but found 2 P1 + 2 P2 + 2 P3: (P1-1) user-shadowable names capture the generated entry/bridge code (bare get/=/assoc/empty? emitted as :variable nodes inside user binders; probed crashes); (P1-2) ordinary assoc mints a working callable — spec 8.10.11 requires entry-spelled source data to REMAIN DATA, and the contradiction is that MY OWN orchestrator brief directed the hand-constructed-descriptor fixture; (P2-1) the direct-apply fallback is value-structural (any entry-less value applies directly), so :yang.call/not-callable is unreachable from source; (P2-2) tail chains through the entry/bridge grow the semantic stack ~9 frames/activation — the slice-4/5 constant-depth invariant was dropped in this diff; (P3s) silent continuation fallback, named-arg errors riding :yang.call/thrown. Escalated (a) the contradiction + (b)-(e) to kimi r4 arbitration (session in collab/1793309600000-*).\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:410:Decisions: P1-2 is an orchestrator-brief vs spec contradiction — my brief's item 5 (hand-constructed fixture) was written by me from the spec's illustrative example, and it conflicts with 8.10.11's remains-data requirement as realized in open Clojure maps; escalated to the section's approving architect rather than resolved by the seat that created the contradiction.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:1:# Session log — yang.clojure track (hardening + adoption of §8.10 common call)\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:35:Done: glm r3 confirmation (session 3e4d9593, resumed after a plan-only stop): N1 CLOSED (all forged shapes refuse with the qualified :yang.call/not-callable via both operators incl. the def-alias route; admitted + dynamic-eligibility intact both lanes), N2 CLOSED (dao.host.gate-test 14/178; manifests 156/154/155, union 168) — \\\\\\\"Ready for Architect sign-off\\\\\\\". astra sign-off r1 DENIED on a real P2 the seat had not caught: the invocation admission gate skipped ARGUMENT evaluation on refusal (§8.10.4 requires operands once, left-to-right, before the callee check) — reproduced on both lanes at 12feb7d1 vs abbfb998. Fix round to kimi -> committed 45269e0f (all operands bound before the witness check, both branches reuse the bindings, refused/admitted regressions both lanes). This seat verified 143/1484 across the five suites + oracle 21/971 + kondo 0 errors. astra SIGN-OFF GRANTED for 63674368..45269e0f, conditions: final-commit shiva Node/Dart lanes + the dao.stream merge gate.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:46:Done: (1) Re-derived the 33-failure regression on the clean rebased tree: bracket GREEN at the rebase base 0dc5d7af (118/0, adoption included), RED from 211dded9 onward — the gate-closure round was authored on the PRE-adoption base and its self-reported green predates the merge. (2) Root cause, measured by probes on both trees: the round introduced a parallel invoker convention — `fn?` stripped of its `yang.call/eligible?` fallback (so `(fn? first)`=false for §8.10 descriptor maps), and a library `invoke-value` (bare `data/callable?` classification → map-lookup branch) wired to a fast path routing ALL local/non-symbol calls through it, so `(f 41)` on a local silently returned nil (get-fallback) and destructuring/update/apply misfired (the 33). (3) Reconciliation (uncommitted): compile-guest-call routes entry-PRESENT callees through admission (admitted→bridged, forged→refused) and entry-ABSENT callees (collections, raw closures) to invoke-value — itself invoked as a proper common call (yang.call/invoke + escape-based raise mirroring bridged's capture/resume); `fn?` restored to the adoption definition; `::invoker` detection tightened to the invoke-value name; the gate round's try/->/fresh-supply/kind-seam work kept. (4) astra r1 (thread 01a199e5) DENIED with two P2 blockers: dispatcher re-entry (apply inside invoke-value recursed into the routing → 30k-instruction exhaustion on scalar/raw-closure callees) and the entry test checking truthiness not presence (`{:yang.call/entry nil}` would lookup). (5) v2: invoke-value refuses via `(throw (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable {...}))` (no apply anywhere), routing test is map-guarded key presence (`(if (data/map? c) (data/contains? c :yang.call/entry) false)`), and new `test-value-invocation-refusals-are-terminating` (library-enabled, walker+semantic): scalar exact-shape refusal, module-fn admission (measured: the linker compiles module fns as ADMITTED descriptors — `(yang.call/entry f)` legitimately succeeds; the projected raw closure refuses), nil/false entry presence refusals, tail-position refusal, operands-before-check in both positions via a guest throw (native refusals escape as host exceptions outside adapter seams — probed and discarded). Focused lane 122/0; kondo 0/0 both files.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:112:Done: (1) The astra design round returned the APPROVED hardening-3 plan (collab/1793770000000-architect-hardening-3-design.gpt-6-astra.*): seven slices — H3-0 restore declared dispositions + trustworthy evidence (lands first, harness-only); H3-1 diagnose the two blocked fixtures (finding: all three blocked C executions hit \\\\\\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\\\\\" at 2,000,000 steps; authorized 2M/4M/8M diagnostic trials, NOT an automatic budget raise); H3-2 proof elaboration (11 arities) via end-to-end proof fixtures starting from the repaired check-assume-have-discharge; H3-3a/b syntax (17) + env/unparser/utils (11); H3-4 presyntax+typing (9; parse/1 direct fixture, poisoned-parse/1 regression preserved); H3-5 normalization (10); H3-6 final audit — independent credit reconstruction from raw traces, 165/165, the (:gate-status) assertion unchanged. Guardrails: executed-arity rule frozen, four departures + two upstream failures stay declared, admission denominator (165/10, 146/9) closed to incidental change, no yang.call/yin.vm changes without a ruling, intermediate sign-offs are not kernel closure, credit withdrawal must always be explained. Two architect findings sharpened the scope: the blocked fixtures' immediate failure is the 2M-step budget (legitimate cost vs repeated work/continuation defects undistinguished), and the deviation classifier is representation-stale (expects a bare closure at :meta; refreshed outcomes carry a §8.10 callable descriptor). (2) H3-0 routed to codex engineering per the plan (worktree h30, brief collab/1793790000000-engineer-h3-0-declared-dispositions.prompt.md): declarations as versioned input, representation-aware classification validated against actual runtime representation (a {:type :closure} map is insufficient), negative controls (mutated call / unrelated id / changed payload / forged representation / incomplete lane), writer round-trip tests, the stale narrative refresh (145/165 and \\\\\\\"only 20\\\\\\\" are dead — 107/58 is the truth), and the expected end state 100/2/2/2 with 107 credited 58 remaining and the gate still :blocked.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:211:Done: (1) With no answer to the lane question, the seat implemented H3-0 directly per the recommendation. Reading the pristine harness revealed the truth the delegates had missed: the ENTIRE H3-0 machinery already exists at HEAD — the classifier `kernel-host-value-deviation` with exact guards and negative-control tests (including the forged-descriptor rejection), `kernel-row` recording `:recorded-deviation` statuses, and the writer emitting `:recorded-portability-boundaries` from classified rows. The SINGLE root cause of the whole regression is astra's r1 finding: the classifier's `(values/closure? meta)` is representation-stale — the reconciled compiler's guest closure at :meta is the admitted §8.10 descriptor map (measured: clojure.lang.PersistentArrayMap with :clj/type :function, :yang.call/entry, :clj/admission), so the check fails, deviations come back empty, the writer honestly records none, and the 2285 assertion fails. The vibe rounds \\\\\\\"fixed\\\\\\\" everything EXCEPT this (round 2 even replaced the working check with an invented shape). (2) The seat's implementation: `kernel-callable-descriptor?` validating the genuine descriptor (function type marker + closure entry + closure admission witness — codebase-true shapes, not invented ones); the classifier accepts either representation; the versioned declarations file drives boundary/upstream-value/reason with revalidation guards (declared message == live message, declared script == live script, normalized); negative controls extended (both representations classify; forgeries — missing admission, non-closure entry, wrong type marker, invented shape — refuse; a mutated declaration fails via with-redefs); the writer gained a `dir` overload so the round-trip test exercises the REAL writer against a temp directory replaying the checked-in evidence (no fixture recompute). The muse round's declarations file was retained as-is (kimi had retained it).\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:222:Done: (1) After the owner left the lane question unanswered, the seat implemented H3-0 directly. Reading the pristine harness showed the ENTIRE machinery existed at HEAD — the single root cause was astra's r1 finding: the deviation classifier's `(values/closure? meta)` was representation-stale (the reconciled compiler publishes the admitted §8.10 descriptor at :meta — measured PersistentArrayMap). The vibe rounds had \\\\\\\"fixed\\\\\\\" everything except this one line's assumption. (2) The seat's implementation: `kernel-callable-descriptor?` (function marker + minted-closure